# Deploy after substantive changes

When you finish **substantive** edits to this repo (app code, APIs, config, migrations):

1. **Commit and push** to `origin` / default branch (`main`) so **Vercel** picks up the deployment. Do not end the task with only local edits if the user expects the live site to update.
2. Use a short, clear commit message describing what changed.
3. If you added or changed **Supabase SQL** under `supabase/migrations/`, remind the user that the **database** must be updated separately (Supabase SQL editor or `supabase db push`), since deploy only ships the app.

Skip auto-push only when the user explicitly asked not to commit, or when there is nothing to commit.
